{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012ad4pjbxrprQeUYMco5zj1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for the \"worst\" tier scenario for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan. Let me carefully analyze the worst tier definition and generate predictions for each experiment.\n\nLet me review the key parameters for the worst tier:\n\n- G3_deploy_ratio_smolvla: [0.82, 0.92] — so compression still helps on SmolVLA/aloha but marginally\n- G3_deploy_ratio_openvla: [1.15, 1.35] — significant degradation on OpenVLA\n- G3_deploy_ratio_libero_avg: [1.1, 1.3] — significant degradation on LIBERO\n\n\n- success_rate_delta_pp: [-15, -5] — success rate drops 5-15 percentage points\n- bound_tightness_ratio_eps001: [15.0, 50.0] — bound is very loose\n- eps001_preservation_rate: [0.85, 0.92] — preservation is okay\n- cross_model_margin_ratio: [5, 20] — margin improvement exists but varies\n- pruned_token_attn_weight_ratio: [0.5, 0.9] — pruned tokens have substantial attention weights\n\nThe narrative direction is shifting away from \"lossless compression\" and \"denoising\" claims toward a \"robustness\" framing instead.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the experimental plan: starting with success rate evaluation on aloha_sim_insertion, then moving through LIBERO and OpenVLA verification, followed by training ablations comparing joint versus gradient-isolated versus two-stage approaches. I'll need to empirically verify the formal bounds, check cross-compression compatibility across different model families, compare defense mechanisms, sweep pruning ratios, analyze token importance patterns, test v8c annealing variants, quantify ACIS overhead, and finally evaluate LIBERO-Plus under 7-dimensional perturbations. Let me work through detailed predictions for each experiment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"u